From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: a restacked top-level keeps its children's frames (1533)

1524 drops the Vulkan frames kept for a window and the windows in it when
it moves, is resized, restacked, shown or hidden, so a pane that moved does
not get its old frame back. The frames are kept relative to the top-level's
X window, so a top-level that only moves or is restacked still has them
where they were. Showing an owned dialog restacks its owner: Outlook's
message body and Word's document went blank behind every dialog ("Want to
save your changes?", Save As, ...) until it closed. A top-level now drops
them only when resized, shown or hidden; child windows as before.

Gate: test/vkchild-gate.sh (new case: the top-level is restacked after its
child presented, then covered; the frame is shown again).
Mutant: SG_MUTANT_VK_TOPLEVEL_RESTACK_DROPS (the restack case fails).

--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
@@ -3340,6 +3340,18 @@
 
     /* Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 1524): child windows' Vulkan frames kept to be
      * shown again (vulkan.c) are not where they were */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_VK_TOPLEVEL_RESTACK_DROPS
+    /* Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 1533): frames are kept relative to the
+     * top-level's X window; a top-level that only moves or is restacked (an
+     * owned dialog opening over it) still has them where they were. Office's
+     * documents and messages went blank behind every dialog until it closed. */
+    if (NtUserGetAncestor( hwnd, GA_PARENT ) == NtUserGetDesktopWindow())
+    {
+        if (!(swp_flags & SWP_NOSIZE) || (swp_flags & (SWP_SHOWWINDOW | SWP_HIDEWINDOW)))
+            vulkan_surfaces_window_changed( hwnd );
+    }
+    else
+#endif
     if ((swp_flags & (SWP_NOMOVE | SWP_NOSIZE | SWP_NOZORDER)) != (SWP_NOMOVE | SWP_NOSIZE | SWP_NOZORDER) ||
         (swp_flags & (SWP_SHOWWINDOW | SWP_HIDEWINDOW)))
         vulkan_surfaces_window_changed( hwnd );
